            <li><span itemprop="itemListElement" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem"><span itemprop="name">  Capacity Building Support for the Philippine Coast Guard (PCG)</span><meta itemprop="position" content="3" /></span></li>
            </ul>
          </nav>
          <!-- //breadcrumbs -->

          <section class="topics topics-article">
            <!-- 記事タイトル -->
            <h1 class="entry-title"> Capacity Building Support for the Philippine Coast Guard (PCG)</h1>
            <!-- 記事投稿時間 -->
            <aside class="topics-article__time">
              <time datetime="2021-3-1">06 October, 2026</time>
            </aside>
            <div class="topics-article__main tich-text">
            <p>Through the JICA framework, the Japan Coast Guard dispatched the MCT and officers from the Coast Guard Research Center to the Philippines to support the enhancement of maritime law enforcement capabilities. There, they provided guidance and advice to PCG criminal investigation instructors and personnel responsible for analyzing marine environmental incidents (such as oil spills and industrial wastewater discharge) on initial investigation and forensic procedures-including on-site preservation, photography, collection of samples and materials, and evidence preservation-as well as evidence collection and analysis related to marine environmental incidents.<br />The JCG will continue to strengthen cooperationand collaboration with the coast guard agencies of other countries to realize a Free and Open Indo-Pacific(FOIP), while also promoting capacity-building support for countries in the Indo-Pacific region.<br /><br /> <a href="upload/EN_sousa260823_29.pdf">Capacity Building Support for the Philippine Coast Guard (PCG)(PDF:665KB)<br /><br /></a></p>
<table border="0" style="height: 900px; width: 850px;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_1.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_1.jpg" width="366" height="274" /><br />Practical training: On-site Investigation</td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_2.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_2.jpg" width="365" height="273" /><br />Practical training: Documentation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_3.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_3.jpg" width="365" height="273" /><br />Laboratory Tour</td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_4.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_4.jpg" width="365" height="273" /><br />Explanation: Oil Sampling Equipment</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_5.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_5.jpg" width="363" height="272" /><br />Practical Training: Forensic Science</td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_6.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_6.jpg" width="360" height="270" /><br />Lecture: Criminal Investigationinto the oil spill incident</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_7.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_7.jpg" width="363" height="272" /><br />Practical Training: Oil Sampling</td>
<td style="text-align: center;"><img alt="sousa_260823_29_8.jpg" src="upload/sousa_260823_29_8.jpg" width="360" height="270" /><br />Strengthen Cooperation:<br />"Investigation" and "Forensic Analysis"<br /><br /></td>
